2	Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
3	Date:   Mon Aug 24 11:22:11 2026 +0300
4	
5	    Fleet dashboard: read the fleet horizontally, one pass at a time (#1314)
6	    
7	    The sweep read a member end to end before starting the next, so the viewer's
8	    rate limit was spent depth-first: the first members got their commit graphs
9	    before the last members were looked at at all, and a ceiling hit mid-sweep
10	    turned the tail of the roster into withheld rows under tiles claiming nothing
11	    was on fire.
12	    
13	    Every member now goes through one pass before any member starts the next —
14	    identity, then attention, then depth, then pack cards, then commit graphs —
15	    so a budget that runs out costs the same panel on every row instead of the
16	    last members entirely. The ordering lives in its own module and the page's
17	    progress line names the pass, since a counter reaching the roster's length
18	    five times over otherwise reads as the page starting again.
19	    
20	    Refs #1311
21	    
22	    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
