{"number":1300,"title":"Build the decision ballot: the park&#39;s checkboxes and the scheduler run&#39;s answer job","body":"The design landed in #1299 (DESIGN §4.1, decision §15.31, scenarios S74–S78). This is the engine half.

What it takes, per the modeled flow:

- a `BALLOT_MARKER` beside the claim/hand-off/episode markers in `queue/work-item.mjs`, and one renderer for a ballot comment (marker + one `- [ ]` per option) so the vocabulary has a single home;
- every parker of a `needs-human-decision` writes one: `queue/converge-item.mjs` / `queue/executor.mjs` for the code-work and hand-off paths, the janitor&#39;s dead-agent rule, and the agent-side instructions in `queue/instructions.md`;
- `planSchedulerRun` gains **job 5**, placed **before job 1** (F32): for each open parked item, read its latest ballot comment after the item&#39;s episode boundary — one tick resumes it (episode marker first, then the status swap), zero waits, more than one comments once and leaves it parked;
- the resumed run reads the chosen option off the item&#39;s own comments, like every other marker.

Nothing here changes the labels, the body fields, or any other job.

